%%label IV. Animé
%%note D flat major. Over a quick shimmer a broad pentatonic tune passes from horns to trumpets; the first movement's theme and call return together; the whole-tone music comes back and rises again to four descending chords; the tune fills the full orchestra, and the call, broadened, leads to a bright ending.
X:1
T:Debussy’s Missing Symphony
T:IV. Animé
C:Lor, in the manner of Debussy
M:6/8
L:1/8
Q:"Animé" 3/8=72
%%score [fl ob eh cl bn] [hn tp] tm {hu hl} [v1 v2 va vc cb]
% The score is written at sounding pitch. Dynamics in the wind, brass and double-bass parts are set one to three levels below the strings to balance the playback samples of this site; they are a playback compromise, not dynamics for live players.
